<!--
  modules/graphic_objects/pom.xml — Stage 2-e Task 2 module POM
  (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-20-stage2e-topo-batch.md).

  STATUS: ADDITIVE and RUN BY HAND (mvn -pl modules/graphic_objects -am
  package from the reactor root, or mvn -f modules/graphic_objects/pom.xml
  package). Ant (modules/graphic_objects/build.xml + build.incl.xml) remains
  the real build; nothing here is wired into CMake or any release build yet.

  WHY THIS MODULE. Seventh in prebuildjava's topo order
  (modules/prebuildjava/build.xml:25), right after action_binding — and by
  far the largest migrated so far (112 source files, 211 .class files, 52
  directory entries in the jar — more directory entries than any other
  module's total non-manifest entry count to date). The FIRST module with
  FOUR simultaneous reactor dependencies at once (action_binding's two was
  the previous high).

  STEP 1 FINDINGS (grep -rhE '^import (org|com|jdk|sun)\.'
  modules/graphic_objects/src/java, 112 files):
    - org.scilab.forge.scirenderer.{ruler.graduations.UserDefinedFormat,
      shapes.appearance.Color} — Datatip.java, XmlSaver.java: reactor
      dependency #1 (scirenderer), below.
    - org.scilab.modules.action_binding.InterpreterManagement —
      Datatip.java: reactor dependency #2 (action_binding), below.
    - org.scilab.modules.commons.{CommonFileUtils, OS, ScilabConstants,
      gui.FindIconHelper, xml.ScilabDocumentBuilderFactory,
      xml.ScilabXMLUtilities} — MenuBarBuilder.java, XmlSaver.java,
      XmlLoader.java, XMLDomLoader.java: reactor dependency #3 (commons),
      below.
    - org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages — Datatip.java,
      MenuBarBuilder.java: reactor dependency #4 (localization), below.
    - org.scilab.modules.graphic_objects.* — itself (in-package, the bulk of
      the 112 files).
    - org.w3c.dom.*, org.xml.sax.* — JDK (java.xml module), not a
      dependency.
  No manifest.class-path anywhere in build.xml: the Ant build left the literal,
  never-interpolated string "${manifest.class-path}" in the jar. RESOLVED
  (register P2, 2026-07-23) — that junk Class-Path line is now dropped from this
  module and the 20 others whose property was never set; the manifest fragment
  below no longer carries it. (gui, javasci and scirenderer keep their real,
  interpolated Class-Path values and are untouched.)

  THE OTHER GENUINELY NEW THING: NO library.title PROPERTY. Every other
  module migrated so far (and every other module in the tree bar
  prebuildjava, confirmed by `grep -L library.title modules/*/build.xml`)
  sets `<property name="library.title" value="..."/>` in its own build.xml.
  modules/graphic_objects/build.xml does not — it sets only library.name.
  Ant's shared `jar` target (build.incl.xml:153) writes
  `<attribute name="Specification-Title" value="${library.title}"/>`
  UNCONDITIONALLY, with no fallback: with the property never set, Ant's own
  manifest task left the literal, un-interpolated string "${library.title}"
  in the built jar. Same FAMILY of bug as the Class-Path/manifest.class-path
  token. RESOLVED (register P4, 2026-07-23) — the manifest fragment below now
  carries a real Specification-Title, "Scilab graphic_objects module": the same
  value as this module's <name> below (build.xml's <description>, the closest
  thing to an authoritative label Ant provides), consistent with every other
  module, where Specification-Title == <name>.

  A THIRD GENUINELY NEW THING, FOUND ONLY BY ACTUALLY COMPILING: Step 1's own
  grep recipe (`^import (org|com|jdk|sun)\.`) is blind to a real dependency
  here. xmlloader/CSSParser.java:17 — a JFlex-generated lexer, "//CHECKSTYLE:OFF"
  and all — carries `@javax.annotation.Generated("JFlex")`, a FULLY-QUALIFIED
  annotation with no import statement at all, so it matches neither the
  "^import" prefix nor the org/com/jdk/sun alternation (it is javax, not one
  of the four). `mvn package` failed outright the first time with "package
  javax.annotation does not exist" before this was added — javax.annotation.*
  was removed from the JDK itself in JDK 11 (it shipped as part of Java EE
  modules, all since removed), so this is a real, non-optional compile-time
  dependency, not a warning. build.incl.xml:104 puts
  ${javax.annotation-api.jar} on the shared compile classpath unconditionally
  (scilab-lib.properties.in:15 -> thirdparty/javax.annotation-api-1.3.2.jar,
  cited against the tracked .in template per modules/scirenderer/pom.xml's
  dependencies comment). Same <scope>system</scope> + <systemPath> mechanism
  as flexdock/jogl/gluegen/rosetta — but UNLIKE those, javax.annotation-api
  IS published under this exact coordinate on Maven Central
  (javax.annotation:javax.annotation-api:1.3.2), used below purely as an
  accurate label; system scope means it is never actually resolved from a
  repository here either.
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
  <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

  <parent>
    <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
    <artifactId>scilab-modules-parent</artifactId>
    <version>2027.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    <relativePath>../../pom.xml</relativePath>
  </parent>

  <artifactId>graphic_objects</artifactId>
  <packaging>jar</packaging>

  <!-- build.xml:20 <description>Build the Scilab graphic_objects
       module</description> — there is no library.title here (see the file
       header comment); this is cosmetic only, never reaching the built jar
       (addDefaultImplementationEntries/addDefaultSpecificationEntries are
       false at the parent, and this module's own manifest section comes
       verbatim from manifestFile below, un-interpolated by Maven). -->
  <name>Scilab graphic_objects module</name>

  <dependencies>
    <!-- Datatip.java imports org.scilab.modules.action_binding.InterpreterManagement. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>action_binding</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- MenuBarBuilder.java, XmlSaver.java, XmlLoader.java, XMLDomLoader.java
         import org.scilab.modules.commons.{CommonFileUtils, OS,
         ScilabConstants, gui.FindIconHelper, xml.ScilabDocumentBuilderFactory,
         xml.ScilabXMLUtilities}. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>commons</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- Datatip.java imports org.scilab.forge.scirenderer.ruler.graduations.
         UserDefinedFormat; XmlSaver.java imports
         org.scilab.forge.scirenderer.shapes.appearance.Color. Same reactor
         coordinate as every other scirenderer-dependent module
         (groupId/artifactId org.scilab:scirenderer per
         modules/scirenderer/pom.xml) despite the org.scilab.forge.*
         PACKAGE namespace scirenderer's classes actually live under —
         the Maven coordinate and the Java package are independent axes. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>scirenderer</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- Datatip.java, MenuBarBuilder.java import
         org.scilab.modules.localization.Messages. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>org.scilab</groupId>
      <artifactId>localization</artifactId>
      <version>${project.version}</version>
    </dependency>
    <!-- xmlloader/CSSParser.java:17 — @javax.annotation.Generated("JFlex"),
         a fully-qualified annotation with no import statement (see this
         file's header comment, "A THIRD GENUINELY NEW THING"). Real Maven
         Central coordinate used as an accurate label; system scope means it
         is never actually resolved from a repository. -->
    <dependency>
      <groupId>javax.annotation</groupId>
      <artifactId>javax.annotation-api</artifactId>
      <version>1.3.2</version>
    </dependency>
  </dependencies>

  <build>
    <!-- build.incl.xml:22 <property name="src.dir" location="src/java/"/>.
         Same source tree Ant compiles — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
         identical comment; nothing module-specific to add here. -->
    <sourceDirectory>src/java</sourceDirectory>

    <plugins>
      <plugin>
        <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
        <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
        <configuration>
          <archive>
            <!-- addMavenDescriptor=false and the Built-By entry are
                 inherited from the parent POM — not redeclared here. Same
                 manifestFile mechanism as modules/localization/pom.xml (see
                 that file's build comment for the full rationale).
                 MANIFEST-section.MF's bytes were EXTRACTED from the actual
                 Ant-built jar's META-INF/MANIFEST.MF (unzip -p
                 modules/graphic_objects/jar/org.scilab.modules.graphic_objects.jar
                 META-INF/MANIFEST.MF), never retyped: Specification-Vendor
                 and Implementation-Vendor both carry the double-mangled
                 "Ã¨" (bytes c3 83 c2 a8) — see modules/localization/pom.xml's
                 fuller comment for the mechanism. Specification-Title carries
                 the literal, un-interpolated "${library.title}" token — see
                 this file's header comment for why that is correct, not a
                 mistake to fix. Implementation-Version is present, frozen at
                 the literal "00000000 0000", positioned between
                 Implementation-Title and Implementation-Vendor exactly where
                 Ant places it. -->
            <manifestFile>${project.basedir}/src/main/manifest/MANIFEST-section.MF</manifestFile>
          </archive>
        </configuration>
      </plugin>
    </plugins>
  </build>
</project>
